  "id": "COMPOUND:24452 - PROTEIN:5837",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Geroquinol may interact with SN12K1, through a series of target interactions involving thioredoxin, a protein involved in mitochondrial function. Geroquinol is shown to target thioredoxin, which is in turn targeted by pseudopterosin Q, rhetsinine, and phorone. All of these compounds are known to interact with thioredoxin, and their shared targeting of thioredoxin implies a common pathway. The final score of 0.5192 across the three paths indicates a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, likely due to the consistent targeting of thioredoxin by multiple compounds. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition of thioredoxin, which may then affect SN12K1 through downstream cellular processes. The evidence supports a plausible, mechanistic link between Geroquinol and SN12K1, though further validation would be needed to confirm the specific role of thioredoxin in this interaction.",
